\begin{theorem}[Algebraic string theory dictionary;
\ClaimStatusProvedHere]\label{thm:algebraic-string-dictionary}
\index{string theory!algebraic dictionary}
The following string comparisons use the specified constructions and comparison data:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\roman*)}]
\item \emph{Filtered chain comparison.}
  For the Kac--Moody and Drinfeld--Sokolov targets, impose all coefficient, square-zero target, filtration, symbol-map, and compatible-correction hypotheses of Theorems~\ref{thm:bar-semi-infinite-km} and~\ref{thm:bar-semi-infinite-w}.
  For a conformal vertex algebra with $c=26$, impose the full separately constructed target, relative descent, section-carrier, filtration, symbol-map, and correction hypotheses of Theorem~\ref{thm:brst-bar-genus0}.
  These data give the stated cohomology comparisons on their specified carriers.
  They are not supplied by the central charge.
  In particular, the augmentation-kernel target for $V\otimes bc$ does not exist by Proposition~\ref{prop:vir-no-augmentation}.
\item \emph{Curvature = conformal anomaly.}
  The obstruction coefficient $\kappa(\cA)$ is the conformal
  anomaly; anomaly duality $\kappa + \kappa' = 0$ holds for
  Feigin--Frenkel dual pairs
  \textup{(}Corollaries~\textup{\ref{cor:anomaly-duality-km}}
  and~\textup{\ref{cor:anomaly-duality-w})}.
  Anomaly cancellation $\kappa_{\mathrm{tot}} = 0$ holds at
  $c = 26$ \textup{(}bosonic\textup{)} and $c = 15$
  \textup{(}superstring\textup{)}.
\item \emph{Genus expansion = string perturbation series.}
  The genus-graded bar complex
  $\barB^{(g)}(\cA)$ is the algebraic $g$-loop
  contribution
  \textup{(}Theorem~\textup{\ref{thm:genus-universality})}.
\item \emph{Factorization = unitarity.}
  The bar complex factorizes at boundary divisors of
  $\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}$, recovering string amplitude
  factorization
  \textup{(}Theorem~\textup{\ref{thm:amplitude-factorization})}.
\end{enumerate}
The genus-zero target, relative descent, symbol maps, and compatible corrections remain required constructions in the stated applications.
Integration pairings require the additional compatibility of Corollary~\ref{cor:string-amplitude-genus0}.
Convergence of the genus series and holographic bulk reconstruction are further mathematical questions.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Each clause references its proof:
(i)~Under the full hypotheses stated in that clause, Theorems~\ref{thm:bar-semi-infinite-km}, \ref{thm:bar-semi-infinite-w}, and~\ref{thm:brst-bar-genus0} sum the compatible corrections to an actual chain quasi-isomorphism;
(ii)~Corollaries~\ref{cor:anomaly-duality-km}
and~\ref{cor:anomaly-duality-w},
Theorem~\ref{thm:anomaly-koszul};
(iii)~Theorem~\ref{thm:genus-universality};
(iv)~Theorem~\ref{thm:amplitude-factorization}.
\end{proof}

